The number of scenarios created is determined by the longest vector
argument. All shorter vectors (including \code{pkmlFilePaths}) are recycled to
match this length.

This allows you to efficiently create multiple scenarios in several ways:
\itemize{
\item \strong{Same PKML, different settings}: Use a single PKML file with vectors
of different parameter values.
\item \strong{Different PKMLs, same settings}: Use multiple PKML files with single
parameter values.
\item \strong{Different PKMLs, different settings}: Use vectors of both PKML files
and parameter values.
